From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LIVI appliance
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:05:00 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: h616: add the Mali GPU (panfrost)

The H616/H618's Mali-G31 MP2 is panfrost-supported through the generic
"arm,mali-bifrost" compatible that 6.12's panfrost already matches; the
node (and its SoC-specific compatible) is the one mainline added for
H616/H618.

The GPU power rail hangs the SoC when the driver touches the registers
with the PRCM power domain still gated (probe printed the clock rates
and wedged, verified on the Zero 2W), so the node carries the upstream
power-domains property and the prcm_ppu node, whose driver is patch
0007. The Zero 2W board dts enables the GPU with mali-supply on the
AXP313A's always-on dcdc1, the same wiring the upstream board dts uses.

panfrost is the arm64 defconfig's =m and the board fragment enables the
PPU it needs; the image does not load the module today (the compositor
stays on llvmpipe/pixman, see README.md "Hardware video decoding"), but
the node plus the power domain are what a Mesa/panfrost image needs, and
they are verified on the Zero 2W: /dev/dri/renderD128 probes and binds
the Mali-G31 with the domain powered.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi                | 21 +++++++++++++++++
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-orangepi-zero2w.dts |  5 ++++
 2 files changed, 26 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
@@ -150,6 +150,21 @@
 		#size-cells = <1>;
 		ranges = <0x0 0x0 0x0 0x40000000>;
 
+		gpu: gpu@1800000 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h616-mali",
+				     "arm,mali-bifrost";
+			reg = <0x1800000 0x40000>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 95 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 96 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
+				     <GIC_SPI 97 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			interrupt-names = "job", "mmu", "gpu";
+			clocks = <&ccu CLK_GPU0>, <&ccu CLK_BUS_GPU>;
+			clock-names = "core", "bus";
+			power-domains = <&prcm_ppu 2>;
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_GPU>;
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		crypto: crypto@1904000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h616-crypto";
 			reg = <0x01904000 0x800>;
@@ -886,6 +901,12 @@
 			#reset-cells = <1>;
 		};
 
+		prcm_ppu: power-controller@7010250 {
+			compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h616-prcm-ppu";
+			reg = <0x07010250 0x10>;
+			#power-domain-cells = <1>;
+		};
+
 		nmi_intc: interrupt-controller@7010320 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h616-nmi",
 				     "allwinner,sun9i-a80-nmi";
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-orangepi-zero2w.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h618-orangepi-zero2w.dts
@@ -93,6 +93,11 @@
 
 /* USB 2 & 3 are on the FPC connector (or the exansion board) */
 
+&gpu {
+	mali-supply = <&reg_dcdc1>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &mmc0 {
 	cd-gpios = <&pio 5 6 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;	/* PF6 */
 	bus-width = <4>;
